["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Ducks put safety first, food second, and they learn fast. Read the flock and you know your next 10 seconds.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Three stages of a flock, a tip. Relaxed: heads down, feeding, tipping up, preening. Alert: necks up and stretched long, holding still, bunching together. Leaving: swimming away, calling, then the flush. If they are alert, freeze; do not take one more step.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Read the flock before it leaves (Tip)</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"380\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"112\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Relaxed</text><g transform=\"translate(160 92) scale(0.9)\"><path d=\"M-30 0 Q-34 -14 -18 -14 L10 -12 Q24 -10 24 0 Q20 10 -2 10 L-22 10 Q-32 8 -30 0Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"28\" cy=\"2\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 4 L44 8 L34 9Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><text x=\"286\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Heads down, feeding,</text><text x=\"286\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">tipping up, preening</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"122\" width=\"380\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"122\" width=\"112\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#d9a23a\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Alert</text><g transform=\"translate(160 174) scale(0.9)\"><path d=\"M-30 0 Q-34 -14 -18 -14 L10 -12 Q24 -10 24 0 Q20 10 -2 10 L-22 10 Q-32 8 -30 0Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"-44\" width=\"7\" height=\"36\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-46\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M22 -48 L33 -45 L22 -42Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><text x=\"286\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Necks up and long,</text><text x=\"286\" y=\"174\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">still, bunching up</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"204\" width=\"380\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"204\" width=\"112\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"247\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Leaving</text><g transform=\"translate(160 256) scale(0.9)\"><path d=\"M-30 0 Q-34 -14 -18 -14 L10 -12 Q24 -10 24 0 Q20 10 -2 10 L-22 10 Q-32 8 -30 0Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"-44\" width=\"7\" height=\"36\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-46\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M22 -48 L33 -45 L22 -42Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><text x=\"286\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Swim away, calls,</text><text x=\"286\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">then the flush</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Alert? Freeze. Do not take one more step.</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Necks up and still: they are about to leave (Tip).</li><li>Freeze the moment you see it (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: alarm signals in detail</summary><ul><li>Relaxed birds feed, tip up, preen and sleep. Alert birds stretch their necks, stop feeding, bunch up and swim away from the threat (Tip, widely reported).</li><li>Hens of most puddle ducks give loud quacks; the whole flock reacts to an alarm (Tip).</li><li>Mallards put safety first, then food, and keep their trips short (80%, Ducks Unlimited research summary).</li><li>Old hand's rule (opinion): \"When the necks go up, your feet stop.\"</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/divers-taking-off.jpg\" alt=\"Divers need a runway, so they leave early.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Divers need a runway, so they leave early. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Waterfowl_Lake_Andes_National_Wildlife_Refuge_South_Dakota_(52781566934).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>No good flush distance numbers for BC ducks (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li><li>Pressured birds flush sooner and farther (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what we know, and what we do not</summary><ul><li>No published flush distance for hunted BC ducks was found. Do not trust a fixed number (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li><li>Divers must run along the water to take off, so they tend to swim off or leave early (Tip).</li><li>Puddle ducks jump straight up, so they often sit tight in cover until you are close, then burst (Tip).</li><li>In a West Tennessee study, ducks disturbed in their sanctuaries \"hunkered down\" and moved less rather than spreading out <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Hunter meaning: on small water, use cover and the bends to get close. On big open water, decoys work better than sneaking (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Map sketch. A refuge lake with no hunting on the left, a grain field or marsh on the right. Ducks fly from the refuge to the food at dusk and back before dawn. GPS tracked mallards made about 2 flights a day and avoided heavily hunted areas during shooting hours, 80 percent. Hunt the line between safety and food, a tip.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hunted ducks: safe by day, food by night</text><ellipse cx=\"90\" cy=\"130\" rx=\"74\" ry=\"50\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".7\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">No hunting</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">refuge</text><rect x=\"250\" y=\"70\" width=\"140\" height=\"110\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#d9c27a\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Grain field</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">or marsh</text><path d=\"M160 104 Q205 70 248 96\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/><line x1=\"240\" y1=\"92\" x2=\"244.85504244572473\" y2=\"94.91302546743484\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"250.0,98.0 243.7,87.2 237.5,97.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M248 156 Q205 186 160 158\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/><line x1=\"168\" y1=\"162\" x2=\"163.14495755427527\" y2=\"159.08697453256516\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><polygon points=\"158.0,156.0 164.3,166.8 170.5,156.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"205\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dusk</text><text x=\"205\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Before dawn</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"212\" width=\"380\" height=\"80\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">GPS mallards: about 2 flights a day,</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">hide from heavy hunting in shooting hours (80%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hunt the line between safe and food (Tip)</text></svg>\n</figure><figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation of a pressured mallard day. During shooting hours the ducks sit tight in a refuge. After legal light ends they fly to a field to feed, feed there at night, and fly back to the refuge before dawn. End card: hunting pressure pushes feeding into the dark, 75 percent.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A pressured mallard day</text><ellipse cx=\"90\" cy=\"160\" rx=\"72\" ry=\"48\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".7\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Refuge</text><rect x=\"260\" y=\"112\" width=\"130\" height=\"96\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#d9c27a\"/><text x=\"325\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Field</text><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"70 150;70 150;300 140;300 140;70 150\" keyTimes=\"0;0.3;0.5;0.75;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"11\" cy=\"-3\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/></g><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"100 168;100 168;330 158;330 158;100 168\" keyTimes=\"0;0.3;0.5;0.75;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"11\" cy=\"-3\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/></g><g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"120 150;120 150;350 140;350 140;120 150\" keyTimes=\"0;0.3;0.5;0.75;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"11\" cy=\"-3\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"0s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"2.7s\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"44\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"67\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Shooting hours: sit tight in the refuge</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"2.7s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"4.5s\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"44\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"67\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">After legal light: fly to feed</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"4.5s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"6.75s\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"44\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"67\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Night: feed in the field</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"6.75s\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"44\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"67\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Before dawn: back to safety</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"9.2s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"252\" width=\"380\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pressure pushes feeding into the dark (75%)</text></g></svg>\n<figcaption>A pressured mallard day. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>GPS (Global Positioning System) mallards avoid heavily hunted areas in shooting hours <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>About 2 flights a day: refuge, food, refuge <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the research</summary><ul><li>West Tennessee, winters 2019 to 2022: GPS tracked mallards \"clearly avoided heavily hunted areas during shooting hours\" and made about two flights a day <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Researchers heard more than 339,000 shotgun volleys over three seasons <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Mallards moved between refuges only if they were less than about 16 km (10 miles) apart <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>In Arkansas, tagged mallards stayed away from public hunting areas for the whole season <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>In heavily hunted areas, ducks rest in no hunting zones by day and fly out to feed at night <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Hunter meaning: hunt the flight line between a refuge and food, at first light and last light (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Week</th><th>Your pond</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Hunt it once, a morning</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Rest it</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Hunt it again</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>\"Ducks perceive sanctuary in weeks, not days\" <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Rest a spot a week or more <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: resting a spot</summary><ul><li>Ducks Unlimited researchers advise that a property may need a week or more of rest to improve hunting <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Short closures (half days, some days off) are a weak substitute for real no hunting areas <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Hunter meaning: you and your brother should have 3 or 4 spots and rotate them (Tip).</li><li>Old hand's rule (opinion, widely taught): \"Never hunt the roost.\" Shooting where they sleep moves them off it.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/mallards-flushing.jpg\" alt=\"Pick one bird. A flock is not a target.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Pick one bird. A flock is not a target. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rainwater_Basin_Wetland_Management_District_(32227957367).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Ducks trust other ducks on the water (Tip).</li><li>That is why decoys work (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: flock behaviour</summary><ul><li>Ducks often land where other ducks already sit; decoys copy that (Tip, the basis of all decoy hunting).</li><li>Mallards in fall flock loosely; teal flocks twist as one; canvasback fly in lines and V shapes <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>A big flock has more eyes. Small groups and singles decoy more easily (Tip).</li><li>Hunter meaning: set decoys in small family sized groups with a clear landing hole (Tip). Spreads: <a href=\"#/s/ducks/16\">Ducks, tactics</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Duck social year, 75 percent. October to November: courtship peaks and drakes display. Early December: over 8 in 10 mallard hens are paired in a wintering study. Spring: the pair flies north and the hen picks the nest. Incubation: the drake leaves within days. Summer: the hen raises the brood alone. Ducks you shoot in fall are often pairs, a tip.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Duck social year (75%)</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"38\" width=\"380\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"38\" width=\"118\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"69\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Oct to Nov</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Courtship peaks, drakes display</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"86\" width=\"380\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#eef2e6\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"86\" width=\"118\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"69\" y=\"113\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Early Dec</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"113\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Over 8 in 10 mallard hens paired</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"134\" width=\"380\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"134\" width=\"118\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"69\" y=\"161\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Spring</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"161\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pair flies north; hen picks the nest</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"182\" width=\"380\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#eef2e6\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"182\" width=\"118\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"69\" y=\"209\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Incubation</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"209\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Drake leaves within days</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"230\" width=\"380\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"230\" width=\"118\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"69\" y=\"257\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Summer</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"257\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hen raises the brood alone</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ducks you shoot in fall are often pairs (Tip)</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Mallards pair up in fall and early winter <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>The drake leaves early in incubation; the hen raises the brood alone <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the social calendar</summary><ul><li>Mallard courtship peaks in October and November in a California wintering study. Over 80% of hens were paired by early December <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>In New York, courtship starts in September and about 90% of hens are paired by November <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Green winged teal pair later: 90% of hens paired by early February <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>The pair flies north together; the hen usually picks the nest site (Tip).</li><li>After a few days of incubation the pair breaks and the drake leaves <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Hunter meaning: in November, drakes and hens often fly as pairs. Name both before you shoot (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two columns. Young birds of the year: on their first trip south, more likely to be shot than adults, 80 percent; they decoy and come to calls easily, a tip. Adults: have seen decoys, circle, look and leave, a tip; late season birds are educated. Opening week has lots of young birds; late season, hide better and call less. Old hand advice, opinion.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Young of the year vs old birds</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"40\" width=\"188\" height=\"170\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f6d7b0\"/><rect x=\"8\" y=\"40\" width=\"188\" height=\"26\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"8\" y=\"54\" width=\"188\" height=\"12\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"102.0\" y=\"59\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Young (this year)</text><text x=\"102.0\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">First trip south</text><text x=\"102.0\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">More likely shot</text><text x=\"102.0\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">than adults (80%)</text><text x=\"102.0\" y=\"143\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Decoy and call easily</text><text x=\"102.0\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(Tip)</text><text x=\"102.0\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"></text><rect x=\"204\" y=\"40\" width=\"188\" height=\"170\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\"/><rect x=\"204\" y=\"40\" width=\"188\" height=\"26\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><rect x=\"204\" y=\"54\" width=\"188\" height=\"12\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"298.0\" y=\"59\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Adults</text><text x=\"298.0\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Have seen decoys</text><text x=\"298.0\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Circle, look, leave</text><text x=\"298.0\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(Tip)</text><text x=\"298.0\" y=\"143\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Late season birds</text><text x=\"298.0\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">are educated (Tip)</text><text x=\"298.0\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"></text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"222\" width=\"380\" height=\"70\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Opening week: lots of young birds (Tip)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Late season: hide better, call less</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">(Old hand advice, opinion)</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Young of the year are shot more than adults <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Late season adults are wary: hide better, call less (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the evidence</summary><ul><li>Bellrose and others (1961): juveniles are more vulnerable to hunting than adults, and the gap varies by place, time, year and species <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>The age ratio in the bag rises after a late nesting year <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>A popular summary says juvenile mallard hens are 2 to 3 times more vulnerable (60%, not checked against the original study). <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li><li>Old hand's rule (opinion): \"Opening week teaches you nothing. December teaches you everything.\"</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 440\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"J hook decoy spread: wind blows from left to right, the main bunch of decoys sits upwind beside the blind, a tail line trails downwind, ducks fly in against the wind and land in the open pocket in front of the blind.\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"60\" width=\"380\" height=\"290\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"85\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Open water</text>\n  <g>\n    <line x1=\"30\" y1=\"32\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"32\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"6\" fill=\"none\"/>\n    <polygon points=\"150,20 174,32 150,44\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n    <text x=\"190\" y=\"38\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">WIND</text>\n  </g>\n  <g fill=\"#6b4f35\">\n    <ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"280\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"6\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"62\" cy=\"255\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"6\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"78\" cy=\"232\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"6\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"96\" cy=\"210\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"6\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"50\" cy=\"228\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"6\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"72\" cy=\"196\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"6\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"102\" cy=\"180\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"6\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"130\" cy=\"166\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"6\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"160\" cy=\"156\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"6\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"192\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"6\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"224\" cy=\"146\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"6\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"256\" cy=\"142\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"6\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"288\" cy=\"138\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"6\"/>\n    <ellipse cx=\"320\" cy=\"134\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"6\"/>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"26\" y=\"312\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Main bunch</text>\n  <text x=\"26\" y=\"328\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">(the hook)</text>\n  <text x=\"250\" y=\"118\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Tail line</text>\n  <ellipse cx=\"190\" cy=\"240\" rx=\"62\" ry=\"40\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 6\"/>\n  <text x=\"190\" y=\"236\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Landing zone</text>\n  <text x=\"190\" y=\"254\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">20 to 25 m out</text>\n  <g>\n    <path d=\"M370 210 Q 320 200 262 228\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/>\n    <polygon points=\"262,228 280,214 282,234\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n    <text x=\"268\" y=\"300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Ducks come in</text>\n    <text x=\"268\" y=\"317\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">against the wind</text>\n  </g>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"350\" width=\"380\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"420\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Shore</text>\n  <rect x=\"150\" y=\"352\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"190\" y=\"372\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You (blind)</text>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"404\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Wind at your side or back.</text>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"422\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Never in your face.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>They land into the wind <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>They return to yesterday's field and flight line (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the habits you can use</summary><ul><li>Landing into the wind: you know which way they will come in <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Same field, same flight line, day after day while the food lasts (Tip, the basis of field hunting).</li><li>They leave to feed earlier on moonlit, windy evenings <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Fresh birds after a cold front decoy easily (65%, hunter lore).</li><li>They trust a calm, spread out flock of decoys on the water (Tip).</li><li>Pressured birds go straight to refuges: the hunter who knows the refuge knows the flight line (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Hook</th><th>Means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>\"Safety, food, short trips\"</td><td>What a mallard wants <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td></tr><tr><td>2 flights a day</td><td>Refuge to food and back <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td></tr><tr><td>16 km</td><td>Refuges farther apart are not linked <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td></tr><tr><td>\"Weeks, not days\"</td><td>How long a spot needs rest <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td></tr><tr><td>\"Necks up, feet stop\"</td><td>Alarm posture (Tip)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Old hand's rule (opinion, widely taught): \"Never shoot the roost.\"</p></aside><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li>\"Young birds dive in, old birds look in.\" Juveniles are more vulnerable <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>; the rest is Tip.</li><li>\"Pairs by December.\" Over 80% of mallard hens paired by early December <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Topic</th><th>Main source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Pressure, refuges</td><td>Ducks Unlimited research 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Pairing</td><td>Canadian Field Naturalist 2021</td></tr><tr><td>Age</td><td>Bellrose and others, 1961</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source, with date checked</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.ducks.org/conservation/waterfowl-research-science/understanding-waterfowl-the-science-of-disturbance\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited, Understanding waterfowl: the science of disturbance (15 January 2026)</a>: GPS mallards, 2 flights, 339,000 volleys, 10 miles, weeks not days, rest a week. Read directly 2026-10-11 (75 to 80%).</li><li><a href=\"https://themeateater.com/hunt/waterfowl/why-do-you-see-so-many-ducks-after-the-season\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MeatEater, why you see so many ducks after the season</a>: Arkansas GPS mallards. Search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://ducks.org/conservation/waterfowl-research-science/ducks-after-dark\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited, Ducks after dark</a>: refuges by day, night feeding, moonlit windy nights. Read directly 2026-10-11 (75 to 80%).</li><li><a href=\"https://canadianfieldnaturalist.ca/index.php/cfn/article/view/2547\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Canadian Field Naturalist, timing of pair formation in three wintering dabblers (2021)</a>. Search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.birdsoutsidemywindow.org/2021/10/26/mallards-are-courting-now/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Birds Outside My Window, mallards are courting now</a>: New York timing. Search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://cawildlife.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/PoTW-9162022.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">California Wildlife Center note</a>: drake leaves after a few days of incubation. Search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://pubs.usgs.gov/publication/70243783\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Bellrose and others, sex ratios and age ratios in North American ducks (1961)</a> and <a href=\"https://wildfowl.wwt.org.uk/index.php/wildfowl/article/view/798\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nesting chronology and vulnerability, Wildfowl</a>. Search preview 2026-10-11 (75 to 80%).</li><li><a href=\"https://greenhead.net/super-hens-the-experts-speak/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Greenhead, super hens</a>: 2 to 3 times figure. Search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://myfwc.com/hunting/waterfowl/hunt-guide/hunt-tips/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Florida Fish and Wildlife Conservation Commission, waterfowl hunt tips</a>: landing into wind. Search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Ducks Unlimited Canada ID guide (flock shapes): see <a href=\"#/s/mc-ducks-01\">Masterclass 1</a> sources <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul></details>"]